			"notes": "First release of **Claude MCP**: a client-side Fabric mod that lets Claude Code, opencode and other MCP clients control your Minecraft client.\n\n## Requirements\n- Minecraft Java **26.3** with Fabric Loader **≥ 0.20.1**\n- [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) **≥ 0.165.0**\n- Java 25 (shipped by the launcher for 26.3)\n\n## Installation\n1. Download `claude-mcp-0.1.0.jar` and put it into your `mods/` folder together with Fabric API.\n2. Start Minecraft once. This creates `config/claudemcp/token.txt`.\n3. Register the server in Claude Code (`register.ps1` from the repo) or add it to opencode as a remote MCP server – see the [README](https://github.com/Hemiize/mc-claude-mcp#quick-start).\n\n## Included (73 tools)\n- **Perception:** state, blocks, entities, inventory, GUI, screenshots\n- **Actions:**\n  - A* pathfinder with drowning protection\n  - mining with automatic tool choice and pickup, placing, crafting via the recipe book, combat, GUI control\n- **Flow:** tasks with emergency stop (`End`) and player override\n- **Memory:** notes and waypoints per world or server\n- **Code inside the game:**\n  - reflection on every class and object of the game\n  - live Groovy scripts and event hooks\n  - runtime method hooks (Java agent + Byte Buddy)\n- **Chat and data:** chat filter for incoming and outgoing messages, NBT editor\n\n## Security\n- The server listens only on `127.0.0.1` and requires a bearer token.\n- Scripts and reflection can be disabled in `config/claudemcp/config.json`.\n- Anti-cheat bypasses are deliberately not included.\n\n## License\nApache 2.0 with **required attribution**: every redistribution must include the `NOTICE` file, which credits Hemiize as the author. It is also bundled in the jar at `META-INF/NOTICE`.\n\n**SHA-256** `claude-mcp-0.1.0.jar`: `7c37b9ebb0970099d2ab1f4ec600b69d42762edd536148effcbbe17102efcd91`"
		}
